 "note": "Geographe Bay Yacht Club, Geographe Bay Rd, Busselton, from docs/landmarks/yacht_club.md (Landgate aerial, OSM outline, club photos). Tan face-brick clubhouse on the dune: the main hall with its low pale roof and a verandah to the bay, the two-storey race tower at the north-west corner (white window band, dark green fascia, G.B.Y.C. in blue letters), the lower solar-panelled wing and entry to the south, the east annex, the 2023 deck with its limestone wall under six blue shade sails, and four teal sails over the BBQ courtyard. The front is the beach (north) side. Signs are plain lettering. Metres: x left to right as seen from the beach (east to west), y back from the hall's north wall (southward).",
